A gold-standard foundational vanilla ice cream tailored specifically for the Ninja CREAMi. Incorporating a single tablespoon of cream cheese creates a natural stabilizer and emulsion, yielding an ultra-dense, velvet-soft scoop without any icy or powdery mouthfeel. Fold in mini chocolate chips during the dedicated mix-in cycle for crunch in every bite.

*Adapted from [Ninja Test Kitchen](https://ninjatestkitchen.com/recipe/vanilla-ice-cream-with-chocolate-chips/).*

## Ingredients

- 1 tablespoon cream cheese, softened to room temperature
- ⅓ cup granulated sugar
- 1 teaspoon pure vanilla extract
- ¾ cup heavy whipping cream
- 1 cup cold whole milk
- ¼ cup mini semi-sweet chocolate chips (chilled, for mix-in)

## Instructions

1. **Create the Emulsion:** Place the softened cream cheese into a medium microwave-safe mixing bowl and microwave on low power for 8 to 10 seconds just to loosen it. Whisk in the granulated sugar and pure vanilla extract with a rubber spatula or small whisk for about 60 seconds. The mixture should become pale, glossy, and resemble smooth cake frosting with no lumps.
2. **Blend the Milks:** Gradually pour the heavy whipping cream into the sweetened cream cheese mixture, whisking continuously to keep it smooth. Pour in the whole milk and whisk steadily for 1 to 2 minutes until all the granulated sugar has fully dissolved and no gritty crystals remain.
3. **Freeze Completely Level:** Pour the ice cream base into a clean Ninja CREAMi pint container. Make sure the liquid does not surpass the embossed MAX FILL line. Firmly secure the storage lid and place the pint on a flat, level shelf in your coldest freezer section. Freeze undisturbed for a full 24 hours (a level surface is essential for the paddle to spin evenly).
4. **Assemble and Spin:** Remove the pint from the freezer and take off the outer storage lid. Insert the pint into the outer bowl container. Secure the Creamerizer paddle into the outer bowl lid and twist the lid into place until locked. Mount the bowl onto the machine base and twist the handle to lock the platform upward. Select the **ICE CREAM** program and let the cycle run to completion.
5. **Add the Mix-In Tunnel:** Once processing finishes, unlock the bowl. Using a spoon or butter knife, carve out a 1 ½-inch wide core directly through the center of the ice cream down to the bottom of the container. Pour the mini chocolate chips into this cavity (it is completely fine if the top elevates slightly above the fill line now).
6. **Process the Mix-In:** Reattach the lid, mount back onto the base, and press the **MIX-IN** button. The paddle will fold and disperse the chips evenly without pulverizing them.
7. **Scoop and Enjoy:** Disassemble the outer bowl and serve the ice cream straight from the pint into chilled bowls.

## Notes

- **If the First Spin Looks Crumbly:** If your freezer runs colder than 0°F (-18°C), the ice cream might appear powdery or crumbly after the first spin. Simply add 1 tablespoon of milk and run a **RE-SPIN** cycle before adding mix-ins; it will turn miraculously silky.
- **Mix-In Swaps:** Swap mini chocolate chips for chopped peanut butter cups, crushed Oreos, or toasted chopped pecans.
